{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'cat /workspace/TASK.md'","aggregated_output":"# Task: H11 — Candidate normalization: stable filter + dedup + ordering\n\n> Held-out RFC-0005 suite · Shape: Collection/data transformation (1/2).\n> You are maintaining an **existing correct system**; do not rewrite it from\n> scratch. Change only what the task requires.\n\n## Base (workspace)\n\nThe workspace contains a correct, deterministic candidate-normalization\nmodule (`h11.dispatch`). Candidates have `id`, `zone`, `score`, `seq`, and\n`active`. The current `normalize` keeps only active candidates and sorts them\nby score descending (ties keep input order); it does **not** remove duplicate\nids and does not apply a secondary tie-break. The program is driven by the\nenvironment variable `H11_SCENARIO` and prints deterministic lines.\n\n## Required change\n\nExtend `normalize` to the full contract:\n\n1. keep only `active = true`;\n2. when the same `id` appears more than once, keep only the **best** record\n   (higher `score` wins; equal score -> smaller `seq` wins; fully identical\n   records -> first occurrence);\n3. order the result by `score` **descending**;\n4. on equal score, order by `seq` **ascending**;\n5. records that rank fully equal must keep their **original stable order**.\n\nThe result still contains multiple distinct ids (this is not a\nbest-candidate pick). Empty input produces the fixed output `EMPTY`.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe hidden verifier drives the compiled program through scenarios (including\npermuted input arrangements) and checks exact output lines: filtering,\ndedup identity, dedup winner selection, primary ordering, tie-break ordering,\nstability, and empty behavior.\n\nThe workspace exposes only the program state and this task; the verifier is\nnot visible to you.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
